            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mcqueenbee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my drink of choice when going out. As a bartender in my 20's, this was your basic cocktail. In bars and restaurants, this is called a madras. From this recipe you build many great drink recipes by adding another liquor (peach schnapps, raspberry vodka, pineapple juice)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mamajean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried this recipe first with 1/2 oz of OJ (could bearly taste the OJ), then with 1 oz OJ, and again with 2 oz OJ. I think GUTK might have meant 1-2 oz OJ. Another way to make with out measuring is 1 part vodka, 1 part OJ and 2 parts cranberry juice.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-02T11:23:21.887Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Beckyshobby"
            },
            "reviewBody": "All the \"summertime\" comments surprised me when this cocktail was included in the Mardi Gras Drinks list. WELL! made it anyway for Fat Tuesday along with Cajun dinner and King Cake. This yummy and light drink totally complemented our Creole menu - in the dead of winter. Doubled the OJ; used pear-flavored vodka (plain or any flavor would be fine); floated frozen raspberries (any frozen fruit will do) Absolutely Addicting and is now part of our year-round rotating cocktail list.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-13T04:24:26.763Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Yoly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Madras is the original name for this drink. It is one of my favorite drinks. The exception I make is I substitute Gold Tequila in place of vodka.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-25T00:04:24.163Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Misty Dean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! I doubled the OJ and used fresh squeezed. I used 100% juice Cranberry juice (no sugar added) from Ocean Spray. It is plenty sweet as it has other juices added for sweetness. I wanted to use orange flavored vodka as one comment suggested, I couldn't find any (the store was out) so I used raspberry flavored and was it ever good!",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-01T07:39:15.767Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Duckball"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like girly drinks and a really strong alcohol taste makes me queasy, so I took the advice of other reviewers and cut down the amount of vodka to about an ounce. I was out of OJ, so I omitted it (next time, I'll be sure to use it!) and I used the Magic Bullet to make it into a slushy drink. It was yummy, even just using the cranberry juice! Thanks, Kim!",
            "datePublished": "2006-02-02T07:57:52.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RayPappy Bailey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "great. but with a vitamix mixer. poured in container, added ice and crushed into a great margarita style drink.",
